      "title": "Modeling Inhibited Growth"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2035fcd0-a2e9-57c4-8a19-382f0eb23461",
      ":question/problem": "The growth of the number of students in a tutoring center is directly proportional to the difference between its maximum capacity and its current population. Let $T(t)$ be the number of students, and let $t\\ge 0$ be the time in months. If the maximum capacity is $301$ students, which differential equation models this population? Assume that $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "11135fac-9bbb-593d-9d9d-cbad003bcaa2",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "2ee5e4b3-c088-56fe-93a4-a6b908ade746",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=k(301-T)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "db38882a-a4bb-5868-bb9c-df24d84a154f",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=kT(301-T)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "d7c9b868-b936-5943-ab57-8e180aa9edab",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=k{T}^{2}(301-T)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "8098ede1-4db2-5f6d-94e4-411eea6cdc52",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(301-T)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "ba11c7cb-1366-52eb-ae95-5b8455acdb2a",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(301+T)"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "2ee5e4b3-c088-56fe-93a4-a6b908ade746"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The rate of change is proportional to the difference between the maximum capacity and the current population. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=k(a-T),\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the maximum capacity and $k>0$.\n\nHere $a=301$ students, so\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=k(301-T).\n$$"
    },
